arc42 chapter titles

The English and German chapter titles of the arc42 template, version 9 (https://arc42.org,
source https://github.com/arc42/arc42-template), as reproduced in README.md, conventions.md,
scripts/checks/routing.py, templates/, tests/ and in the documentation sets this skill generates, were created, maintained and (C) by Dr. Peter Hruschka, Dr. Gernot Starke and
contributors. They are licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0
International License (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/), not under the MIT
license. The licensors provide the template as is; see Section 5 of that license.

Changes: the titles appear verbatim or in sentence case, and as file names converted to lower
case with hyphens and umlauts transliterated (e.g. "05-bausteinsicht.md"). Three English titles
deviate from the original wording: "Constraints" (Architecture Constraints), "Crosscutting
concepts" (Cross-cutting Concepts) and "Risks and technical debt" (Risks and Technical Debts).

Software Guidebook chapter structure

The Software Guidebook chapter structure is by Simon Brown, described in "The Software
Guidebook" (https://leanpub.com/documenting-software-architecture). It is not published under an
open license. The chapter canon follows an earlier edition that includes an External Interfaces
chapter, which the current edition no longer has. The German chapter names are this project's
own translation.
